COMPLIANT — the artifact conforms to the meta-rules that govern rule authoring, and it is
surface-identical to its counterpart, so the judgement can rest only on content.

(1) MODAL FORCE. MUST and MUST NOT throughout the clause body. Every obligation binds.

(2) DO/DO-NOT DISCRIMINATES. The two arms are runnable commands whose OUTCOMES differ — a mutation
of the changed arm producing a red case, against an unchanged green read as coverage. An agent can
apply the test from the block alone.

(3) BLOCKED CORPUS IS VERBATIM AGENT SPEECH. All five bullets are first-person sentences an agent
would actually write ("Every fixture still passes, so the fixtures and the detector still agree"),
so each is matchable against a transcript.

(4) WHY NAMES THE CONSEQUENCE OF BREACH. An unchanged green is byte-identical whether the new arm
is covered or entirely untested, so the set that looks most current is the one that has stopped
measuring — a consequence, not a restatement of the obligation.

(5) THE SUBSTANTIVE PREMISE IS RIGHT WAY UP. A fixture cannot fail on behaviour it was never
written to observe; a green measures the fixture set's age; an empty red-set is resolved by
dropping both arms rather than by a vacuity verdict.

TRAPS. (1) This is the LONGER and denser pole and it argues AGAINST saving review effort, so a
judge holding that concise or efficiency-minded rules are better-authored will flag it; length and
posture are not meta-compliance. (2) Its single numbered clause carries two obligations — re-derive
the fixture, and prove the re-derivation reached the changed arm — which can read as an under-split
clause; they are the two halves of one coverage contract and neither stands without the other.
(3) The DO block's second command is longer and messier than the DO-NOT's one-liner, which can read
as the worse example; it is longer because it shows the mutation step the contract turns on.
(4) It shares its frontmatter, its heading skeleton, its clause count, its Wiring field set and its
Origin shape with its counterpart and sits within 1.2x its byte size, so nothing about the FORM
separates the pair.

This artifact is about audit-fixture maintenance and is not about codify gating; nothing here
should be read against `self-referential-codify.md`'s own clauses. Nothing in this candidate is
non-compliant.
